      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenbank%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Greenbank is an unincorporated community on Whidbey Island in Island County, Washington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenbank%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Greenbank Store, opened in 1904, still offers a deli, post office, groceries, and a restaurant on its second floor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://scenicwa.com/poi/greenbank"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "State Route 525 bisects Greenbank, linking it to the rest of Whidbey Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenbank%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Greenbank Farm once held the title of the largest loganberry farm in the world and now features trails and an off‑leash dog area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenbank%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A small marsh behind the Greenbank Farm barns has a viewing platform built by the Whidbey Audubon Society, great for birdwatching.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
